summary:
- topic: Grievance Denial
  text: Following an executive session, the Board voted to deny a grievance and directed
    the superintendent to provide written notice to the Grievant and the union.
- topic: Student and Staff Recognitions
  text: The meeting celebrated numerous achievements, including the Boys' Track Class
    A State Championship, individual music student honors, and the induction of CraigSkeffington
    into the MaineMusicEducatorsAssociation Hall of Fame. The SPHSRoboticsTeam also
    received a $5,000 grant from ConsolidatedCommunications.
- topic: Community Partnerships Report
  text: Gretchen McCloy and Brenna Latham presented a detailed report on community
    engagement, highlighting nearly 500 volunteers, significant donations of food,
    shoes, and coats, and successful career exploration programs for students across
    all levels.
- topic: Federal Title Funding Update
  text: Dr. Prince provided an update on Federal TitleFunding/ESEA for FY25, noting
    a significant decrease in Title I funds for the district. Plans were outlined
    for allocating the remaining funds to support literacy, math intervention, social
    work, multilingual students, and professional development.
- topic: Facilities Bond Referendum Discussion
  text: The Superintendent presented a proposal for a bond referendum up to $17 million
    to address school safety, deferred maintenance, and SPHS athletic facilities.
    The discussion included a focus on the environmental impact and recyclability
    of artificial turf options for the stadium.
- topic: Bond Referendum Resolution
  text: The Board voted to direct the administration to prepare three separate bond
    referendum proposals, not exceeding a total of $17 million, to allow for independent
    consideration of school safety, deferred maintenance, and athletic facilities
    improvements.
- topic: Finance Committee Report
  text: The FinanceCommittee reported the district is in good fiscal health with 15%
    of the budget remaining for the last 8% of the year. The committee also acknowledged
    findings from the recent auditor's report and committed to addressing them.
